From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:50:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: seal the spike's logins' and cards' keys with the
 vault's key

Fenix kept the two keys in SecureAbove22Preferences, which a release
stores in plaintext beside the stores. The spike keeps them sealed with
AES-256-GCM under the browser's key from the vault, each bound to its
name, and committed rather than applied. Nothing is read or written
until the vault has given the key: the stores wait for it, and a read
without it throws rather than answering that nothing is stored.

The gate saves, lists and deletes a login and a card of the spike's
own, and asks for the logins before the vault is open, to see when
they arrive (encri-firefox W6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
